        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>returns the position of the point d.pt relative to the sphere, resolving &quot;exactly on the
sphere&quot; ties into Inside or Outside by simulation-of-simplicity as described at the inSphere
overload above, using the ids of d and of the points given in reset()
(never returns OnSphere or NoSphere);
shall be called only after reset() returned true, and all four ids must be distinct
</verbatim> </para>
        </detaileddescription>
