        <type>bool</type>
        <definition> bool mrmeshpy.InSphereTesterSoS.reset</definition>
        <argsstring>(self, PreciseVertCoords a, PreciseVertCoords b, PreciseVertCoords c, int rSq)</argsstring>
        <name>reset</name>
        <qualifiedname>mrmeshpy.InSphereTesterSoS.reset</qualifiedname>
        <reimplements refid="classmrmeshpy_1_1InSphereTester__int_1a7a357715850841b696a919571dfc51ff">reset</reimplements>
        <param>
          <type>self</type>
          <defname>self</defname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classmrmeshpy_1_1PreciseVertCoords" kindref="compound">PreciseVertCoords</ref></type>
          <declname>a</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classmrmeshpy_1_1PreciseVertCoords" kindref="compound">PreciseVertCoords</ref></type>
          <declname>b</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classmrmeshpy_1_1PreciseVertCoords" kindref="compound">PreciseVertCoords</ref></type>
          <declname>c</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>int</type>
          <declname>rSq</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>prepares the tester for the sphere of radius sqrt(rSq) passing via points a.pt, b.pt, c.pt,
with the center located on the positive side of their plane (in the half-space pointed at by
cross( b.pt - a.pt, c.pt - a.pt ) from the plane), remembering the ids for the queries;
returns false if no such sphere exists: the points are collinear or coincident,
or rSq is less than the squared circumradius of the triangle;
this hides the id-less reset of the base class, which would leave stale ids
</verbatim> </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
